# The AGS app is its own repository — https://github.com/mohrefaey-creator/ags_edusmart,
# named in apps.json — kept apart because it is MIT and the upstream it sits on
# is AGPL. It lives here as a working checkout so scripts/bootstrap.sh can
# install it without a network round-trip, but this repo does not track it.
#
# Two consequences that are easy to miss, because both were:
#   * a commit here NEVER includes a change under apps/. Commit and push the app
#     from inside apps/ags_edusmart, or the change exists only on this disk.
#   * a fresh clone of this repo has no application in it. CI checks the app
#     repo out into apps/ags_edusmart before building; the VM runbook clones
#     nothing because it pulls the built image.
apps/

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
node_modules/
.env
*.log
.DS_Store
sites/
brief.json

# Stray Redis dump from a local run.
dump.rdb

# k6 writes these next to the profile on every run (handleSummary). The results
# worth keeping are the curated load-tests/results-*.txt, not the raw dumps.
load-tests/k6/summary.json
load-tests/k6/calibration.json
deploy/compose/.env
